# Mobile UX

Phone is the primary device. Build the 380px view first. Desktop is the adaptation, not the baseline.

---

## The bugs that break every hand-built PWA

Fix these once, globally, before building screens. Each one is invisible in a desktop browser and obvious the moment you open the app on a phone.

```css
html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }

/* 1. 100vh is wrong on mobile. Browser chrome is not accounted for */
.app-shell { min-height: 100dvh; }

/* 2. Bottom nav sits under the iOS home indicator without this */
.bottom-nav { padding-bottom: max(var(--s-2), env(safe-area-inset-bottom)); }
.app-header { padding-top: max(var(--s-3), env(safe-area-inset-top)); }

/* 3. iOS zooms the whole page when focusing an input under 16px */
input, select, textarea { font-size: 16px; }

/* 4. Grey flash on every tap */
* { -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; }

/* 5. Pull-to-refresh fires while scrolling a sheet */
body { overscroll-behavior-y: contain; }

/* 6. Momentum scroll trapped inside modals */
.sheet-body { -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; }

/* 7. Text selection on tap-and-hold of buttons and rows */
button, .ledger-row { user-select: none; }
```

In `index.html`:
```html
<meta name="viewport"
      content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#EEF1F4"
      media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#101317"
      media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)">
<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
```

`viewport-fit=cover` is required or `env(safe-area-inset-*)` always returns 0.

