## Layout

- **Bottom tab bar, 5 items maximum:** Dashboard, Ledger, Transfers, Budget, More. Fixed, 56px plus safe area, `--surface` with a top hairline. Icon plus `--t-micro` label. Active state is the icon filling in and the label going to `--ink`, not a coloured pill.
- **Thumb zone:** primary actions live in the bottom third of the screen. Destructive and rarely used actions live top-right. Never put the main action in a top-right corner on mobile.
- **Full-bleed lists:** the ledger runs edge to edge with internal padding. Do not put a 16px-margined card around a scrolling list on a 380px screen. It wastes 8% of the width for decoration.
- **One column, always.** No side-by-side layouts below 768px. No horizontal scrolling tables, ever. If data does not fit, restructure it into rows.
- **Sticky context:** the ledger's date header sticks. The dashboard's period selector sticks. Nothing else sticks.

---

## Touch and gesture

- Minimum target 44x44px, including invisible padding around small icons.
- Minimum 8px between adjacent targets.
- Everything reachable by tap. No hover-only affordances, no right-click menus, no tooltips as the sole source of information.
- **Swipe actions on ledger rows:** left reveals Recategorise, right reveals Mark as transfer. Threshold 40% of row width, with haptic-style visual snap. Always also available in the row detail view, because swipe is undiscoverable on its own.
- **Long press** on a ledger row enters multi-select for bulk actions.
- **Pull to refresh** on Dashboard and Ledger triggers a sync. This is the one gesture users will try unprompted.
- **The transfer review queue is the highest-volume interaction in this app.** It gets: full-width cards, swipe right to confirm, swipe left to reject, undo toast for 5 seconds after each, and a visible counter. The user will clear 50+ of these after the first bulk import. If it takes more than one gesture per item, the feature has failed.

