## Sheets, not modals

Every overlay on mobile is a bottom sheet, not a centred dialog.

- Drag handle at the top, drag-to-dismiss, backdrop tap to dismiss
- Snap points where useful: half-height for filters, full for detail
- Sheet content scrolls; the sheet itself does not
- Confirm actions pinned to the bottom of the sheet, above the safe area
- Use the same component for: transaction detail, filters, category picker, account picker, date range

Use `<dialog>` with `showModal()` for focus trapping, styled as a sheet. Do not hand-roll focus management.

---

## Forms and input

- The category picker is a searchable sheet, never a native `<select>` with 40 options.
- Amount inputs use `inputmode="decimal"`, never `type="number"` (spinners, scroll-wheel changes, and locale bugs).
- Date inputs use the native picker on mobile.
- The CSV import mapping screen is the hardest thing to fit on a phone. Render it as a vertical stack of field cards, one per mapping, each showing the target field name, a dropdown of source columns, and a live preview value from row 1. Not a table.
- Validate on blur, never on keystroke. Error text sits beneath the field in `--signal`.

---

## Feedback

- Every write action gets an optimistic update plus a toast. Toast sits above the bottom nav, not over it.
- Destructive or bulk actions get an **Undo** toast for 5 seconds rather than a confirmation dialog. Fewer taps and safer.
- Only genuinely irreversible actions (delete account, wipe data) get a typed-confirmation dialog.
- Offline: a persistent thin bar under the header, `--caution`, reading "Offline. Showing data from 2h ago." Import buttons disable with the reason shown inline, not a silent failure.
- Never a full-screen blocking spinner. Skeletons that match the final layout.

---

## Performance on a phone

- Virtualise the ledger from the first commit (`@tanstack/react-virtual`). Multi-year, multi-account history is tens of thousands of rows and an unvirtualised list will jank on a mid-range Android.
- Lazy-load the Sankey and all chart code. Recharts plus d3-sankey is a large chunk and the Dashboard should paint before it arrives.
- Target: interactive in under 2s on a throttled 4G Moto G-class device. Test with Lighthouse mobile, not desktop.
- Images: none. This app has no photography. Any decorative image is a mistake.

---

## Accessibility floor

Not optional, and most of it is free if done from the start.

- Visible focus ring on every interactive element: `outline: 2px solid var(--flow); outline-offset: 2px`
- Category colour is never the only signal. Always paired with a text label
- Contrast: 4.5:1 for body, 3:1 for large figures. Check `--ink-faint` on `--surface-2` specifically, it is the pair most likely to fail
- `aria-live="polite"` on the toast region and the sync status
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
- All amounts get an `aria-label` with the full spoken value, since `−42.50` is read badly by screen readers

